  "body": "This PR is stacked on #2331. Its base is `issue/2201-frame-caches`. Retarget it to `main` before #2331 merges.\n\n## What changed\n\nCost row 1 of #2201. The UI computed `operation::status_of` (the full generation stamp) for each operation on each frame. This now occurs only when the world changes.\n\n- `schema::WorldRevision` and `app::world_rev` (new). Two flecs observers move one revision on each `OnAdd`, `OnSet` and `OnRemove` of each component. One observer is for the wildcard id and one is for the wildcard pair. Each move takes a fresh number from one process counter, so two worlds never share a value. The read-time memos `GeoSig` and `GeomPrintMemo` do not move it.\n- `operation::status_shown` and `operation::stale_reason_shown` (new, `status_memo.rs`). These keep the answer of `status_of` / `stale_reason` for each operation until the revision moves.\n- These UI readers use the cached reader:\n  - the browser tree row\n  - the stale count in the status bar (`panes.rs`)\n  - the operation page status and stale reason\n  - the debug panel\n- These callers keep `status_of`, the uncached truth:\n  - generation\n  - verify\n  - the collision checks\n  - the post, `posting_sim` and the post dialog\n  - `RegenerateAll`\n  - MCP and the script API\n- `SetSetupPostScriptOptions` wrote `SetupDef` in place (`get::<&mut SetupDef>`). That write sends no event. It now clones and `set`s.\n- Row 7: `op_page.rs`, `state.rs` and `shell.rs` read the toolpath through `model::with_toolpath`. They do not clone it.\n\n## The key and its writers\n\n`status_of` reads only world components. Each writer of these components uses `set`, `add`, `remove` or `destruct`. Thus the observer covers each writer:\n\n- each command `apply` and `invert` (undo and redo)\n- the generation result and `ClearToolpath`\n- the verify results (in `Toolpath.warnings`)\n- the tool, stock, setup, machine and model edits\n- project load (into the same world or a new world)\n- entity delete\n\nThe decision file `docs/decisions/2201-status-cache.md` has the full table. The test `no_component_is_written_in_place` scans `app` and `ui` and fails on a new in-place component write (`&mut` terms, `ensure_mut`, `get_mut::<`).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/status_cache.rs` (10 tests):\n  - `still_frames_compute_each_status_once` (the build count)\n  - `reads_never_move_the_revision`\n  - `an_operation_param_edit_rebuilds_and_undo_redo_follow`\n  - `a_tool_edit_and_a_tool_delete_rebuild`\n  - `generate_and_clear_rebuild`\n  - `stock_model_and_placement_edits_rebuild`\n  - `a_prior_operation_edit_rebuilds_the_next_one`\n  - `setup_machine_and_delete_rebuild`\n  - `a_project_load_rebuilds`\n  - `no_component_is_written_in_place`\n  - Each test also asserts that the cached value equals `status_of` and `stale_reason`.\n  - Mutation check: with the observer store disabled, 6 of the tests fail.\n- `frame_cost_ops_probe`: still frames with 1 and 8 operations compute no status (`statuses: 0` for f1, f8, g8 and n8).\n\n## Readings (debug, fig8.step, 6 still frames, `frame_cost_ops_probe`)\n\n| State | ui before | ui after | scene before | scene after |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| f1 one toolpath, selected | 8.68 ms | 2.46 ms | 2.67 ms | 2.40 ms |\n| f8 eight toolpaths, one selected | 12.10 ms | 2.59 ms | 2.72 ms | 2.59 ms |\n| g8 eight toolpaths, all shown | 12.78 ms | 2.65 ms | 3.24 ms | 2.89 ms |\n| n8 eight toolpaths, none selected | 11.30 ms | 1.85 ms | 2.54 ms | 2.34 ms |\n\nIn f1, `ui/browser` went from 3.43 to 0.53 ms. `ui/status` went from 2.89 to 0.06 ms. In f8, `ui/browser` went from 5.24 to 0.68 ms, and `ui/status` went from 4.30 to 0.06 ms.\n\n## Gates (debug, `-j 4`)\n\n- app tests:\n  - `status_cache` 10\n  - `commands_undo` 30\n  - `post_script_options` 7\n  - `operations` 120\n  - `project_roundtrip` 73\n  - `setups` 12\n  - `stock_stamp` 4\n  - All pass.\n- `camcraft-ui --lib`: 1024 pass, 6 ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Release timings.\n- The GUI exe (not started).\n- The `crates/ui/tests/` integration binaries.\n- The MCP and script paths (unchanged, they call `status_of`).\n- Snapshot PNGs (not changed).\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: The operation tree, status bar and operation page no longer compute each operation's status again on each frame. A still frame with eight operations draws the UI about four times faster.\n\nRefs #2201\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
